7913 | Page 255 | {} | 1105 PM  Macon Ga May 13 1865  / 11 AM 13th Qr Mr Genl ---- Gen Molineaux reports from / Augusta only three feet six inches water in the Savannah / I fear there will be great difficulty in supplying my / command by that line and would suggest if we / are to remain in Ga that the Chattanooga & Atlanta / RR be opened I can put three thousand men to / work at once & with a very slight expense for / labor can soon have the road in running order ---- / aside from Military considerations I know nothing which / would do more good reestablishing the relations of Ga with the / loyal states than reconstruction of this important line of / communication sig J. H. Wilson Bvt Maj Gen /  /  / 11 10 PM  Nashville May 13 1865  / Nash ---- May 13th 9 PM ---- Secy War ---- I have reliable  / information that GC Torbett Prest & John A / Fisher cashier Bank of Tenn are now at / Augusta Ga with the books & assets of said / bank deposited in the vaults of the Bank of / Augusta also that JT Dunlap TE / R Way and Joel A Battle are at Augusta / having in their custody the archives of the / state of Tenn carried off by order of Ex - Gov Harris / & all the locomotives & a large number of cars / belonging to the Nashville & Chattanooga RR I would suggest orders be  / sent to the officer in command at Augusta to immy / arrest the above named parties & seize the property / books funds & RR rolling stock & hold subject to the  / requisition at the Gov of the state of Tennessee ---- GH Thomas MG /  / 
